Right - priests are great for these reasons, but I don't play them any
more since I ascended with a priest.  Why waste time doing that when I
could be notching up a win with a different character class?  For me,
it's barbarian and priest down, the rest to go :-)

After trying (quite) a few archeologists with no success so far, I've
been seeing how I go with wizards lately.  As a wizard, it can be
tough to survive the first few levels, but sometimes they start out
with some great items.  My favourites are rings of regen, conflict,
and levitation is useful in later stages (or in the early stages if
you want to levitate over your engraving so it won't rub out).
A wand of speed monster or inviz is pretty groovy too.

A question: I want to win without any form of cheating.  How much of
a cheat is polypiling?  I just want to know what you hack-heads out
there think; obviously there can't be any absolute rule about this.
If you don't like to polypile, what constitutes a polypile - one
item? 5? 100?  One could argue that all polypiling is OK, since the
ability to do it is built into the game (unlike restoring save files),
but it _is_ mentioned in the "abuse" section of the spoilers. Opinions?

